    789  f486							; SelectActiveObject — MOVED from bank0 (C1, 2026-10-20; was $F5D5-$F6F6).
    790  f486							; Entry: bank0 VBL `jsr CallPad_SelectObject` ($FC1D `sta $1FF8`) -> the fetch
    791  f486							; at $FC20 is THIS bank's `jmp SelectActiveObject` (see the pad note at $FC20).
    792  f486							; Every exit tail-jmps ReturnPad ($FBF8 = `sta $1FF6`; bank0 serves the `rts`),
    793  f486							; so the VBL frame is popped exactly once and nothing is pushed here.
    794  f486							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    795  f486							; Chosen GRP1 object for this frame; the TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so objects
    796  f486							; flicker by rotating slots. Sets ObjBase, ActiveObjectX, ActiveObjectY,
    797  f486							; ObjTop and COLUP1 (plus P1's hardware X via SetObjectXPos_b2).
    798  f486							; Slot count (enemies + miner?) lives in Temp for this VBLANK only.
    799  f486							; Bomb fuse (state=1): low-priority — bomb only when (BombTimer&3)==0 (~15 Hz);
    800  f486							; other frames normal miner/enemy rotation (FlickerFrame alone).
    801  f486							;
    802  f486							; What changed vs the bank0 body (behaviour identical):
    803  f486							;   * the enemy TYPE is a direct `lda (EnemyDataLo),Y` — the room records are
    804  f486							;     level data in THIS bank, so the FoldIndirect hop (25c, 2 switches) and
    805  f486							;     the FetchPtr staging are gone;
    806  f486							;   * the room-dark test is INLINE: bank1's IsRoomDark ends in `jmp ReturnPad`,
    807  f486							;     which would land back in bank0 and strand this frame. Same mask split and
    808  f486							;     same Z contract; tools/test_room_dark.py drives BOTH bodies and asserts
    809  f486							;     they agree for rooms 0-9 and every split bit;
    810  f486							;   * SetObjectXPos / fineAdjust / SetObjReflection / the two type tables are
    811  f486							;     local copies at $F800 (bank0 ROM is not visible from here).
    812  f486							; ==============================================================================
    813  f486					      .ds	$F486 - *, 0
    814  f486				   SelectActiveObject
    815  f486							; Tally / frozen scene (DropTarget = $FE): show the PLAYER and the MINER
    816  f486							; only — no enemies, no raft, no bomb. That frame bypasses the overscan, so
    817  f486							; RefreshEnemyY never runs while bank1's HUD writes $E0-$EF: EnemyRamY
    818  f486							; ($E2-$E4) is left holding score-pointer bytes, and any enemy drawn then
    819  f486							; jumps to a garbage Y (user report 2026-10-18: the raft "moved up to the
    820  f486							; middle of the screen" the moment the points counting started).
